window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["2f"]={"https://theconversation.com/view-from-the-hill-backpacker-compromise-another-example-of-albanese-government-folding-its-cards-296271":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"dc7a5d5eb3a8f4681f6dd8f4ba916a5312abc090301ee5116301e80056f6b1e4","read":"https://theconversation.com/view-from-the-hill-backpacker-compromise-another-example-of-albanese-government-folding-its-cards-296271","bytes":177266,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"View from The Hill: backpacker compromise another example of Albanese government ‘folding its cards’","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T08:13:20Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Home Affairs Minister Tony Burke on Tuesday sought to remove yet another political irritant, when he announced an overhaul of the government’s new rules for working holiday makers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government was following a course that has many names. John Howard’s chief of staff Arthur Sinodinos famously used to talk about scraping off “barnacles”. The media loves the label “backflips”. Anthony Albanese would no doubt prefer the more benign-sounding “changing our position”."]},{"k":"p","s":["It all amounts to one thing – cutting or limiting losses when a decision becomes a severe political problem. A policy decision is announced, there’s a backlash from vested interests and or the wider community. The government hangs tough for a while, then it gives in and modifies or abandons its original plan. Sometimes trouble in the Senate is in the mix. Sometimes change follows consultations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Politically, the trick is, in the words of ",["The Gambler","https://youtu.be/7hx4gdlfamo"],","]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ve got to know when to hold ‘em"]},{"k":"p","s":["Know when to fold 'em"]},{"k":"p","s":["Know when to walk away"]},{"k":"p","s":["And know when to run."]},{"k":"p","s":["On backpackers, Burke is stepping away from details of his original version while insisting the regions will be better off under his revamp, but the Net Overseas Migration (NOM) won’t be affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under his latest model, the number of first year backpackers has been slowed, but the number allowed a third year is increased, while the number of hours worked in the regions will be boosted overall. The ballot announced originally has been modified and renamed an “invitation”."]},{"k":"p","s":["The opposition sees a con. Time will tell whether the policy works, in terms of labour force and the politics."]},{"k":"p","s":["The point is, the government came under pressure from stakeholders and the present mood is to respond where possible, rather than let unpopular decisions fester."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was the same on a very different front: the sell-off of surplus defence properties. There was a hoo-ha about the planned sale of the historic Victoria Barracks in Sydney, with Defence Minister Richard Marles misjudging the mood when he said, “It’s not my priority to see Defence manage the oldest wine cellar in Australia. It’s nice that it’s at Victoria Barracks Sydney, but it’s not core interest in terms of defending the country.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["After a campaign against the sale, the government declared Victoria Barracks and some other high-profile properties were to be taken off the list."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier, after a big campaign from critics, the government retreated from a proposed $5,000 cap on support for allied health services for veterans."]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget tax changes have seen plenty of concessions made."]},{"k":"p","s":["When the Australian Taxation Office announced it would ban the use of credit cards to pay tax bills, the government backed it briefly, then stepped in to cover the cost of delaying the measure until mid next year while there were further consultations. You can bet there will be some workaround at the least."]},{"k":"p","s":["In October, the government retreated from a plan to split disaster recover funding with the states on a 50-50 basis, which would have left them worse off."]},{"k":"p","s":["The big outstanding decision with a question mark over its durability is the budget measure that will cut the extra rebate older Australians get on their private health insurance cover. The Greens say they will only pass it if pensioners are excluded. The saving is put at $3 billion over the budget period; a carve out of pensioners would take $1.6 billion."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government has to decide whether to try to stare down the Greens, at the risk of forfeiting all the savings, or get what it can by compromising."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many backtracks cost the budget a greater or lesser amount. In the case of the health insurance rebate, there would be a cost in retreating – and an even bigger one, if the Greens held out, in not retreating."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the words of the song go,"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every gambler knows"]},{"k":"p","s":["That the secret to survivin’"]},{"k":"p","s":["Is knowin’ what to throw away"]},{"k":"p","s":["And knowin’ what to keep."]}],"chars":3858},"https://theconversation.com/myanmars-el-nino-threat-shows-why-extreme-heat-is-also-a-question-of-inequality-294870":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"6aa9b17e88606bb1c85b3a8a642d6a26782f343c6310006cc66f10b1f5939d7b","read":"https://theconversation.com/myanmars-el-nino-threat-shows-why-extreme-heat-is-also-a-question-of-inequality-294870","bytes":180778,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Myanmar’s El Niño threat shows why extreme heat is also a question of inequality","by":[{"n":"Hein Thu","r":"PhD candidate, National University of Singapore"},{"n":"Shahmir Hassan Ali","r":"Assistant Professor of Public Health, National University of Singapore"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T03:11:26Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A historically strong El Niño is underway. US forecasters expect ",["a strong to very strong event to continue into early 2027","https://www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/products/analysis_monitoring/enso_advisory/ensodisc.shtml"],". In Myanmar, ",["meteorologists","https://www.gnlm.com.mm/prepare-early-to-meet-super-el-ninos-challenges/"]," warn that its effects could extend into the hot season from March to May."]},{"k":"p","s":["Forecasts can estimate how high temperatures will rise. But they cannot predict who will become ill or die. That depends not only on the weather, but also on people’s ability to protect themselves."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Myanmar, though, widespread hardship does not mean equal risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["After years of conflict, displacement and unreliable electricity, extreme heat will deepen existing inequalities. The ",["International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC)","https://www.ifrc.org/document/heat-through-eyes-most-vulnerable-perceptions-and-pathways-action"]," warns that heat can disrupt electricity, water and healthcare, especially where conflict has damaged infrastructure. The ",["UNHCR","https://www.unhcr.org/sites/default/files/2024-11/no-escape-unhcr-climate-report-2024.pdf"]," highlights displaced people’s greater climate risks due to inadequate housing and essential services."]},{"k":"p","s":["Myanmar is not alone. Three in four people displaced by conflict live in countries ",["highly exposed to climate hazards","https://www.unhcr.org/media/no-escape-ii-way-forward"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why extreme heat is especially dangerous in Myanmar"]},{"k":"p","s":["The human body cools itself mainly through sweating. When temperatures and humidity remain high, this process becomes less effective, putting extra pressure on the heart and kidneys. The World Health Organization (WHO) warns that ",["extreme heat can worsen","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/climate-change-heat-and-health"]," cardiovascular disease, diabetes, asthma and kidney disease."]},{"k":"p","s":["High nighttime temperatures are particularly dangerous because the body needs cooler conditions to recover. Without relief after sunset, the risk of heat-related illness increases."]},{"k":"p","s":["Myanmar’s electricity supply has deteriorated since the military takeover in February 2021. Power cuts have ",["become more frequent during the dry season","https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/myanmar/publication/in-the-dark-power-sector-challenges-in-myanmar"],", when falling hydropower reservoir levels reduce electricity generation while demand for cooling rises."]},{"k":"p","s":["The pressure emerged early this season. Starting Oct. 5, the Ministry of Electric Power and Energy introduced ",["rotating power cuts","https://elevenmyanmar.com/news/power-to-be-distributed-on-rotational-basis-starting-october-5"],", citing El Niño-related heat that had pushed electricity demand beyond available supply."]},{"k":"p","s":["The consequences go beyond losing access to fans and air conditioning (AC). Electricity is also needed to pump clean water, refrigerate medicines and operate medical equipment. ",["A 2023 US modelling study","https://pubs.acs.org/esthag/article/57/22/8245/399320/How-Blackouts-during-Heat-Waves-Amplify-Mortality"]," found that a multi-day blackout during a heatwave could more than double heat-related deaths."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although the exact impact may differ in Myanmar, this highlights an important point: electricity is a public health resource during extreme heat."]},{"k":"h","s":["Who bears the greatest health risks?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Social epidemiologists identify ",["three ways social disadvantage affects health","https://academic.oup.com/book/26479/chapter/194919341"],": exposure, vulnerability and consequences. All three are evident in Myanmar."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, exposure is unequal. Farmers, construction workers and day labourers often continue working during the hottest hours because losing a day’s income is not an option."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wealthier households, meanwhile, can invest in solar-powered cooling such as fans or AC to stay safe during grid blackouts. One industry estimate suggests that household solar installations increased from ",["a few hundred in 2019 to around 300,000 in 2025","https://www.reuters.com/sustainability/climate-energy/war-torn-myanmar-embraces-solar-tackle-power-crisis-2025-11-14/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["With the global fuel shock ",["pushing inflation to 24.6% in April 2026","https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2026/06/16/myanmar-s-economy-shows-tentative-stabilization-but-fuel-shock-intensifies-pressures"],", that protection is slipping further out of reach for poorer households. Rising heat stress also ",["threatens workers’ livelihoods and productivity","https://www.ilo.org/resource/news/increase-heat-stress-predicted-bring-productivity-loss-equivalent-80"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, vulnerability differs. Older people, young children, pregnant women and people with chronic illnesses face greater health risks during extreme heat. WHO estimates that heat-related deaths among people aged over 65 increased ",["by about 85%","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/climate-change-heat-and-health"]," between 2000–04 and 2017–21."]},{"k":"p","s":["Third, the consequences depend on access to treatment. Heatstroke requires rapid cooling and medical attention. Survival may depend on access to transport, functioning clinics, medical equipment and electricity. These are precisely the resources that poor and displaced communities are least likely to have."]},{"k":"h","s":["How conflict widens the protection gaps"]},{"k":"p","s":["Conflict does not flatten these inequalities; it sharpens them. As of July 2026, nearly 3.8 million people ",["were internally displaced","https://www.unocha.org/publications/report/myanmar/myanmar-humanitarian-update-no-52-13-july-2026"]," in Myanmar. Many live in temporary shelters with ",["limited access to clean water and healthcare","https://www.unocha.org/publications/report/myanmar/myanmar-humanitarian-update-no-52-13-july-2026"],". Plastic roofs, overcrowding and poor ventilation leave them particularly exposed to extreme heat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare access is also increasingly difficult. The humanitarian organisation Insecurity Insight recorded ",["at least 1,939 attacks","https://myanmar.un.org/en/318595-myanmar-health-cluster-bulletin-june-2026"]," on healthcare between Feb. 2021 and May 2026. Ongoing fighting and movement restrictions further limit humanitarian organisations’ ability to deliver medical assistance."]},{"k":"p","s":["For an older woman with heart disease living in a displacement camp, the risks are compounded. She has no fan, limited drinking water and no nearby functioning clinic. Her age, illness, gender and displacement each add to her risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["These disadvantages can reinforce one another, an example of ",["intersectionality","https://chicagounbound.uchicago.edu/uclf/vol1989/iss1/8/"],", a concept used by health equity researchers to explain how overlapping social disadvantages drive poorer health."]},{"k":"p","s":["No study has yet measured these combined effects in Myanmar, where weak death registration also makes heat-related deaths difficult to identify and count."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Epidemiologist Geoffrey Rose","https://academic.oup.com/ije/article-abstract/30/3/427/736897"]," argued that the causes of illness in an individual are not necessarily the same as the factors driving disease across a population."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Myanmar, temperature may explain why someone becomes ill on a particular day. But poverty, displacement and electricity shortages explain why entire communities face greater risks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why heat preparedness may fail"]},{"k":"p","s":["The military-backed government has begun ",["opening heat shelters","https://elevenmyanmar.com/news/yangon-opens-over-600-heat-shelters-to-counter-super-el-nino-threat"]," in Yangon. But a shelter only protects people who trust it and feel safe enough to reach it."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Young people have been seized","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c680zlny0gk4o"]," at checkpoints and in public places under the military’s conscription law. Displaced communities have also faced military attacks, including reported ",["airstrikes on displacement camps in Rakhine State","https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/myanmar-military-airstrikes-rakhine-displacement-camps-kill-eight-rebel-group-2026-10-05/"],". For people living in areas affected by military operations, travelling to an officially designated shelter may itself involve risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also a political and administrative challenge: ",["no single authority","https://thediplomat.com/2026/07/does-myanmar-still-have-one-government-to-recognize/"]," controls all of Myanmar. Ethnic armed organisations and resistance groups administer large parts of the country. Yet most heat plans assume a single government that issues warnings and runs clinics. A plan delivered through the military-backed government alone is unlikely to reach many communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the climate warms, Myanmar is a preview for other conflict-affected countries such as Sudan and Yemen, where stronger heat is arriving just as protections are falling apart. Even in a crisis, suffering is not shared equally, and treating crisis-hit populations as one group hides those most at risk. The heat is shared; the harm is not."]}],"chars":6732},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/australia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"018a991fa3ed890077bed81bb54c583b49cf3caf476ecca5d782faf50a9f3e56","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/australia","bytes":75872,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Australia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-19T14:06:09+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Bushfires in Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a higher risk of bushfires in Australia during the spring and summer seasons, from October to February. For advice, visit the bushfires section on the ",["safety and security page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/australia/safety-and-security#bushfires"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/australia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Australia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Australian High Commission in the UK","https://uk.embassy.gov.au/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Australia, your passport must be valid for the length of your planned stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling through or transiting another country on your way to or from Australia, check the entry requirements for that country. Many countries require at least 6 months validity remaining on your passport, even if you’re just in transit and do not pass through immigration."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British- Australian dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British-Australian dual national, you must leave and enter Australia on your Australian passport. You could face difficulties and delays if you do not. See ",["Australian government advice for dual nationals","https://smartraveller.gov.au/guide/dual-nationals.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Australia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["British citizens can usually get the following types of electronic visitor visa:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["eVisitor visa","https://immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/evisitor-651#Overview"]," – there is no visa application charge or service fee"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Electronic Travel Authority (ETA)","https://immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/electronic-travel-authority-601"]," through the ",["iOS app","https://apps.apple.com/au/app/australianeta/id1527982364"]," or ",["Android app","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=au.gov.homeaffairs.eta&hl=en_AU&gl=US"]," – there is no visa application charge, but there may be a service fee"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Department of Home Affairs has ",["information on all other types of visas","https://immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-finder"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Australia, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],". See the Australian Department of Health’s ",["information on yellow fever for travellers","https://www.health.gov.au/resources/publications/yellow-fever-fact-sheet"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Australia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/15/australia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Australia","https://www.smartraveller.gov.au/while-youre-away/biosecurity-border"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Quarantine rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia has strict quarantine rules to keep out pests and diseases that could affect plant, animal or human health."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must fill in an ",["Incoming Passenger Card","https://www.abf.gov.au/entering-and-leaving-australia/crossing-the-border/at-the-border/incoming-passenger-card-(ipc)"]," and either:"]},{"k":"li","s":["declare goods considered to be a risk, such as food, animal products and plant material (including wooden articles)"]},{"k":"li","s":["dispose of goods in bins at the airport or seaport"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must also declare if you have ‘been in contact with farms, farm animals, wilderness areas or freshwater streams/lakes etc in the past 30 days’."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Australian authorities X-ray luggage. They inspect, treat and, if necessary, confiscate and destroy items of concern. You can get a heavy fine if you break quarantine."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Department of Agriculture has more information on quarantine rules."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Australia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. You should be vigilant, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["In December 2025, 15 people were killed in an antisemitic terrorist attack at Bondi Beach, Sydney."]},{"k":"p","s":["In April 2024, several people were injured in a terrorist incident at a church in Wakeley, Sydney."]},{"k":"p","s":["See the ",["Australian government’s national terrorism threat level","https://www.nationalsecurity.gov.au/national-threat-level/current-national-terrorism-threat-level"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take precautions to protect yourself from petty crime, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not leaving your bag or luggage unattended"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping luggage out of sight in cars"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping valuables and passport in a hotel safe"]},{"k":"li","s":["leaving copies of important documents with family and friends in the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["carrying a photocopy of your passport for ID"]},{"k":"li","s":["being particularly careful at night in busy tourist areas"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are many different types of scams targeting people in or travelling to Australia, including dating and romance scams, websites offering fake services or building repair scams. You can check current scams or report your concerns about a scam on the ",["government’s scamwatch website","https://www.scamwatch.gov.au/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can reduce the risk of losing your passport by carrying a proof of age card – this could be a driving licence or a student ID. This is accepted ID for many services like opening a bank account or entering licensed premises."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Laws on smoking and e-cigarettes (vapes) differ between states. The Australian government is reviewing laws, so the rules may change. You must have a prescription to buy e-cigarettes containing liquid nicotine. There are ",["strict rules on importing vaping goods","https://www.odc.gov.au/importers/importing-vaping-goods-australia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In all states it is illegal to smoke in enclosed public spaces. Get local advice on any restrictions, and see ",["smoking and tobacco laws in Australia","https://www.health.gov.au/topics/smoking-vaping-and-tobacco/about-smoking/laws-in-australia"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some drinks served in bars in Australia can be stronger than those in the UK. Alcohol and drugs can lead to you being less alert, less in control and less aware of your environment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Australian authorities act against anyone who imports or traffics illegal drugs. Prosecution can lead to a lengthy prison sentence and deportation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex marriages are legally recognised. Australia is generally open-minded about homosexuality, but there are isolated incidents of homophobic crime. Visit Gay Australia is a useful travel planning resource alongside ",["LGBT+ information from the Australian Human Rights Commission","https://humanrights.gov.au/our-work/lgbti"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mobile phones"]},{"k":"p","s":["The mobile phone network generally works well in cities and large towns, but coverage elsewhere can be very limited or non-existent. If you’re travelling to remote areas, check with your phone provider about coverage. You can use your UK mobile phone in Australia if global roaming has been activated, but making and receiving calls can be expensive. Many visitors prefer to buy an Australian SIM card on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use any Telstra public payphone to make free phone calls to Australian numbers. Free wifi is also available at some payphones around the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Working holidays"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Australia on a working holiday visa, the ",["Fair Work Ombudsman","https://www.fairwork.gov.au/"]," website has information about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your rights as an employee in Australia"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to report any concerns about unfair or unlawful treatment online – you can also call 131 394"]},{"k":"p","s":["Different tax rules and rates apply to residents and non-residents. Working holidaymakers are usually regarded as non-resident for tax purposes. This means they do not qualify for any tax-free personal allowance on earnings. Get guidance from the ",["Australian Taxation Office","https://www.ato.gov.au/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["information for people working in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-australia#working-in-australia"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rip currents are the main hazard for all swimmers and surfers. They can happen at any beach and can sweep even the strongest swimmer out to sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow guidance on ",["beach safety in Australia","https://beachsafe.org.au/surf-safety"]," and tips from ",["Surf Life Saving Australia","https://sls.com.au/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals have been injured diving into water that was too shallow. Make sure there is sufficient depth of water before diving, and always follow warning signs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Diving and snorkelling safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Snorkelling accidents can happen and have sometimes been fatal."]},{"k":"p","s":["You are required by law to complete a medical declaration for diving or snorkelling at a resort. For your own health and safety, you must be truthful about any medical conditions you have."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dangerous wildlife"]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia has many dangerous animal species. There are crocodiles, jellyfish, sharks, venomous insects, spiders and snakes in many parts of the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["See Beachsafe’s ",["information on dangerous marine creatures","https://beachsafe.org.au/surf-safety"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Walking and hiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to walk or hike, research the area you’re visiting and prepare for the terrain and weather, including intense heat. It can take hours to get help in an emergency in the bush or national parks. There is advice on bush safety on each state or territory’s government website. See:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["New South Wales","https://www.police.nsw.gov.au/safety_and_prevention/safe_and_secure/outdoors"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Queensland","https://parks.des.qld.gov.au/experiences/bushwalking/walk_safely.html"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Victoria","https://www.police.vic.gov.au/outdoor-and-bush-safety"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Western Australia","https://parks.dpaw.wa.gov.au/know/bushwalking"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Northern Territory","https://pfes.nt.gov.au/emergency-service/public-safety-advice/natural-disaster-advice/heatwaves"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["South Australia","https://www.police.sa.gov.au/your-safety/crime-prevention-and-security/safety-and-security-tips"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Tasmania","https://www.parks.tas.gov.au/?base=5576"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Australia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Australia if you remain a temporary overseas visitor. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to stay in Australia and have a permanent visa, you can drive using your UK licence for up to 3 months. To continue driving, you must get an Australian licence within this 3-month period."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving laws and regulations differ in each state and territory. Driving under the influence of alcohol or drugs is illegal. The penalties can be severe. You must always wear a seat belt. See the ",["Australian Road Rules","https://www.ntc.gov.au/laws-and-regulations/australian-road-rules"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must carry your driving licence and passport when driving. Make sure you have sufficient insurance, including if you borrow a car from a friend or relative."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hire cars"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re hiring a car immediately on arrival, be cautious about driving. You might be jetlagged and tired from your flight. Take regular rest breaks at the many rest stops on the roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car insurance often does not cover driving on unsurfaced roads. Check your policy before you set off."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia is known for having large distances between towns and amenities."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you have enough water before travelling"]},{"k":"li","s":["tell someone about your plans"]},{"k":"li","s":["check road conditions before starting"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay with your vehicle if it breaks down"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the weather forecast – avoid travelling in extreme heat or severe weather"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sudden storms and strong winds can make driving difficult."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care when driving on unsurfaced roads, 4-wheel-drive tracks and desert or beach roads. Northern Territory Police have warned tourists to stay off unsurfaced tracks in remote areas of Central Australia, following reports of stranded motorists."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving in the outback"]},{"k":"p","s":["Prepare thoroughly if driving in remote outback areas, which can present unexpected hazards. To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a roadworthy vehicle fitted with GPS and 2 spare tyres"]},{"k":"li","s":["take good maps and extra food, water and fuel"]},{"k":"li","s":["plan your route carefully and get local advice before you set out"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave your route details and expected time of return with the local tourist authorities, police, your hotel or hostel, or friends and relatives, and let them know when you’ve arrived safely"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving on K’gari (Fraser Island)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following a number of serious accidents, all vehicles on K’gari (Fraser Island) must not drive faster than 80km/h on beaches and 30km/h in towns. Four-wheel-drive vehicles must have no more than 8 occupants, including the driver. You must store all luggage inside the vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid driving at night and be aware of beach hazards like ditches created by the surf. K’gari is remote and emergency services can take many hours to reach an accident. Carry a well-stocked first-aid kit and personal medication as there is no pharmacy on the island. The Queensland government has more ",["information on keeping safe in K’gari","https://parks.des.qld.gov.au/parks/kgari-fraser"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bushfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bushfires can occur in any part of Australia, including areas close to towns and cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of the risk of bushfires, especially at the height of the Australian summer from November to February. Bushfires can start and change direction and become a risk to life very suddenly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia regularly battles devastating bushfires. Previous fires resulted in the loss of lives and property with many residents and visitors advised to evacuate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Australian authorities have a range of online information and apps to help citizens and visitors keep track of weather and bushfire warnings. You should consider downloading weather and emergency information apps from the Australian or State governments:"]},{"k":"li","s":["‘ BOM Weather’ – all-Australia weather forecast and warnings ."]},{"k":"li","s":["‘Hazards near me’ – New South Wales"]},{"k":"li","s":[["‘VicEmergency’","https://emergency.vic.gov.au/prepare/#where-do-i-get-information-in-an-emergency"]," – Victoria"]},{"k":"li","s":[["‘AlertSA’","https://www.alert.sa.gov.au/"]," – South Australia"]},{"k":"li","s":["‘ ",["EmergencyWA’","https://news.dfes.wa.gov.au/media-releases-feature-stories/feature-story-emergency-wa-app/"]," – Western Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in or near an affected area, follow the advice of local authorities:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Australian Capital Territory Fire and Rescue"]},{"k":"li","s":[["New South Wales Rural Fire Service","https://www.rfs.nsw.gov.au/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["Northern Territory Fire and Rescue Service"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Queensland Fire and Emergency Services","https://www.qfes.qld.gov.au/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["South Australian Country Fire Service"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tasmania Fire Service"]},{"k":"li","s":["Victoria’s Country Fire Authority"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Western Australia Department of Fire and Emergency Services","https://dfes.wa.gov.au/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Bushfires can cause poor air quality and aggravate respiratory conditions. Smoke can accumulate far from a fire, including in urban areas and major cities. If you’re unable to avoid smoke affected areas, state and territory governments monitor air quality and give advice:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Australian Capital Territory","https://www.health.act.gov.au/about-our-health-system/population-health/environmental-monitoring/monitoring-and-regulating-air"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["New South Wales","https://www.dpie.nsw.gov.au/air-quality"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Northern Territory","https://nt.gov.au/environment/environment-data-maps/air-quality-monitoring"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Queensland","https://apps.des.qld.gov.au/air-quality/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["South Australia","https://www.epa.sa.gov.au/data_and_publications/air_quality_monitoring"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Tasmania","https://epa.tas.gov.au/epa/air/monitoring-air-pollution/real-time-air-quality-data-for-tasmania"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Victoria","https://www.epa.vic.gov.au/EPAAirWatch"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Western Australia","https://www.wa.gov.au/service/environment/environment-information-services/air-quality"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Heatwaves"]},{"k":"p","s":["Extreme heat is a serious risk in Australia. See the Australian Red Cross’s ",["information on heatstroke and heat exhaustion","https://www.redcross.org.au/emergencies/prepare/heatstroke-and-heat-exhaustion/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rain and tropical cyclones can cause flooding, including flash floods in some areas. You can get flood warnings from the Bureau of Meteorology. Check ",["local media reports","https://www.abc.net.au/emergency/?nw=0"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Significant weather events can happen suddenly. Spillways, flood plains and drains can quickly become submerged."]},{"k":"p","s":["The local authorities may issue stay-at-home or leave-now orders. Always follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["More information can be found on the relevant state and territory websites:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Australian Capital Territory","https://esa.act.gov.au/be-emergency-ready/floods"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["New South Wales","https://www.ses.nsw.gov.au/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Northern Territory","https://depws.nt.gov.au/water/water-resources/flooding-reports-maps"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Queensland","https://www.getready.qld.gov.au/understand-your-risk/types-natural-disasters/flood"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["South Australia","https://www.ses.sa.gov.au/flood/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Tasmania","https://www.service.tas.gov.au/services/emergencies/emergency-alerts/check-current-flood-warnings"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Victoria","https://www.ses.vic.gov.au/plan-and-stay-safe/emergencies/flood"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Western Australia","https://www.dfes.wa.gov.au/site/flood/overview.html"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["While rare in Australia, earthquakes can happen. Follow the advice of the local authorities and emergency services in the event of a natural disaster."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclones affect some parts of Australia, mainly Queensland, Northern Territory and Western Australia. The cyclone season normally runs from November to April."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local and international weather updates from the World Meteorological Organization and the Australian Bureau of Meteorology."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in or near an affected area, follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dust storms"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dust storms happen regularly in Australia, usually only in outback areas. Follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 000 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Australia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/15/australia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Australia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/15/australia#General_Information"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Japanese encephalitis and other insect or tick-borne diseases"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["While you are in Australia, you can access essential and urgent medical care through the UK-Australia Reciprocal Healthcare Agreement. Find out more about ",["healthcare for UK citizens in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-reciprocal-healthcare-agreements-with-non-eu-countries#australia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Essential and urgent hospital treatment is free. There is a charge to visit GPs and receive prescriptions. You can recover some costs through Medicare, Australia’s universal health insurance scheme. You can ",["enrol with Medicare through Services Australia","https://www.servicesaustralia.gov.au/reciprocal-health-care-agreements-visiting-from-united-kingdom?context=22481#a3"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re not covered by reciprocal healthcare arrangements between Australia and the UK, costs of treatment can be high."]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of healthcare in Australia is very good. UK residents are entitled to limited subsidised health services from Medicare for medically necessary treatment while visiting Australia. These provisions do not apply to non-visitors, for example those studying in Australia. Other exclusions under the reciprocal agreement include pharmaceuticals (unless you’re in hospital), use of ambulance services and medical evacuations, which are very expensive."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more ",["information on medical services in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/australia-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 000 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Australia"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Australia"]," in Australia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information/australia-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/australia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/australia/british-high-commission-canberra"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/australia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-australia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":20760,"change":"Updated information about global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/guilfoyle-resigns-as-ambassador-to-greece-adding-to-the-global-vacancies-sapping-us-embassies-294315":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"bd3cd33554813f376a2f7e29a539161273563ae940aa99413413bfda42ba0bf0","read":"https://theconversation.com/guilfoyle-resigns-as-ambassador-to-greece-adding-to-the-global-vacancies-sapping-us-embassies-294315","bytes":183412,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Guilfoyle resigns as ambassador to Greece – adding to the global vacancies sapping US embassies","by":[{"n":"Donald Heflin","r":"Executive Director of the Edward R. Murrow Center and Senior Fellow of Diplomatic Practice, The Fletcher School, Tufts University"}],"pub":"2026-10-13T18:02:11Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The United States is down one more ambassador. On Oct. 13, 2026, it emerged that President Donald Trump had asked Kimberly Guilfoyle, a MAGA loyalist and ex-fiancée of Trump’s son Donald Jr., to ",["resign her position as U.S. ambassador to Greece","https://apnews.com/article/trump-ambassador-greece-guilfoyle-9da9d2e50e18bccc38946404c1ca756f"],", a NATO ally. It follows allegations that the Trump adviser turned diplomat pushed for a Republican donor to ",["pay off her six-figure American Express bill","https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/guilfoyle-amex-donor-100-000-0e02cdc3"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Guilfoyle later confirmed that she would comply with the request ",["and resigned","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/13/us/politics/kimberly-guilfoyle-resign.html"],". In so doing, Athens became one of a number of U.S. overseas missions with a vacancy at the top. In fact, ",["93 out of 196 U.S. ambassador jobs","https://afsa.org/list-ambassadorial-appointments"]," are currently unfilled."]},{"k":"p","s":["And that is after ",["U.S. senators confirmed 10 new ambassadors","https://www.senate.gov/pagelayout/legislative/one_item_and_teasers/nom_confc.htm"]," before leaving town on Sept. 30, 2026. Among those nodded through before Congress closed for an extended midterm recess were new U.S. ambassadors for Kenya, Nicaragua, Malaysia and Kyrgyzstan."]},{"k":"p","s":["With some of the vacancies the White House has not even sent names to Capitol Hill, despite the second Trump administration being a year and a half into the job. With others, the Senate, which is controlled by the same party as the White House, hasn’t acted on the names put forward. Should the Athens position be added to the list, the reason will be down to potential insufficient vetting or an ill-advised appointing strategy that promotes loyalty over experience."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regardless of the reason, as a ",["former ambassador and an expert in the process of diplomacy","https://sites.tufts.edu/murrowcenter/leadership/"],", I find the current vacancies concerning. Among those embassies still without a top person in place are key partners for the U.S. – countries that Washington needs to achieve its security, economic and strategic objectives."]},{"k":"p","s":["What makes these vacancies more worrying, in my view, is that they come amid other concerning developments in the State Department’s staffing of embassies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Politicizing diplomacy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Chief among them are the ",["high percentage of politically appointed ambassadors","https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/08/06/trump-fills-ambassador-posts-with-more-donors-loyalists-than-any-recent-president/"]," relative to positions filled by career diplomats – that is, senior foreign service officers, usually with at least 20 years of diplomatic experience."]},{"k":"p","s":["Though many countries send politicians abroad as ambassadors, America’s diplomatic service is unique in two ways. The percentage of U.S. ambassadors who are political appointees – those who haven’t followed a career civil service path – is ",["higher than comparative countries","https://doi.org/10.1093/ia/iiae116"]," across the world. Second, those political appointees are ",["often donors with little to no government experience","https://theconversation.com/trumps-insistence-on-personal-loyalty-from-ambassadors-could-crimp-us-foreign-policy-273087"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The practice has existed for decades, but in recent years the ",["number of political appointees has increased","https://afsa.org/appointments-barack-obama"],". During the Obama administration, the percentage of political appointees was around 30%. The number rose to around 40% in the first Trump administration and the subsequent Biden administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["But in Trump’s second term, some ",["80% of names the White House has sent","https://afsa.org/appointments-donald-j-trump-2nd-term"]," to the Senate have been political."]},{"k":"p","s":["And many of the people Trump has put forward don’t appear to have the credentials usually associated with holding important diplomatic positions. Rather, ",["many are friends, associates or donors","https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/08/06/trump-fills-ambassador-posts-with-more-donors-loyalists-than-any-recent-president/"]," to Trump, often with little overseas experience or knowledge of the country they are going to."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lee Lipton, ",["ambassador to a key ally in the Philippines","https://ph.usembassy.gov/ambassador-lee-lipton/"],", is owner of a restaurant in Palm Beach – Florida Benny’s on the Beach – a member of Trump’s Mar-a-Lago Club and a contributor to his political campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["The system of political appointees has always had an element of handing ambassadorships to friends and supporters. But what has changed under Trump is the range of positions now available. In the past, ambassadors to key countries like Chile, Israel, Peru, the Philippines, Turkey and Egypt, for example, have almost always been career appointees. This has changed under the second Trump administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Appointing noncareer diplomats to small, faraway nations has the additional problem that the chosen individual may not actually spend much time there. The rule of thumb has long been that ambassadors should spend no more than one month every year back in the United States. But that is compromised if a noncareer diplomat with expansive business ties in the U.S. is selected."]},{"k":"h","s":["The role of a deputy"]},{"k":"p","s":["A closely related problem is the State Department’s handling of an ambassador’s second in command, their ",["deputy chiefs of missions","https://afsa.org/current-deputy-chiefs-mission"]," – DCMs for short – under Secretary of State Marco Rubio."]},{"k":"p","s":["During Trump’s first term in the White House, politically appointed ambassadors were often ",["encouraged to swap out the DCMs","https://theconversation.com/trumps-insistence-on-personal-loyalty-from-ambassadors-could-crimp-us-foreign-policy-273087"]," they inherited from their predecessors. It meant going through a long hiring process, leaving those key jobs unfilled for months."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2025, the State Department went further, canceling the assignments of senior officers ",["en route to take up embassy jobs","https://www.nbcwashington.com/news/national-international/trump-removes-nearly-30-career-diplomats-from-ambassadorial-positions/4032589/"]," and opening a new hiring process."]},{"k":"p","s":["It formed part of a Trump purge of what many MAGA Republicans ",["characterized as a “deep state” civil service","https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/23/trump-administration-recalls-30-ambassadors-promote-loyal-diplomats"],". The reality is that DCMs ",["fill a critically important role","https://diplomaticacademy.us/2024/12/29/advice-for-political-ambassadors/"]," in helping political appointees navigate the bureaucracy and implement their policy ideas, as well as raising the occasional reality check."]},{"k":"p","s":["With more politically appointed ambassadors – some of them with no relevant experience – having an experienced DCM can be the difference between success and failure."]},{"k":"h","s":["Looking for other friends"]},{"k":"p","s":["When you put all of these personnel changes together, the result is the degradation of what was once seen as one of the most effective diplomatic services in the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["What makes this potentially more worrying is where the vacancies are. For example, Belarus and Bulgaria, neighbors to Russia and Ukraine, are without U.S. ambassadors. And important countries in the fight against terrorism or in geopolitical hot spots, such as Kuwait, Qatar and Mauritania, are in the same camp."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other countries still without ambassadors include Indonesia, Southeast Asia’s largest nation and the most populous Muslim-majority country in the world; key Middle East ally Egypt and nuclear power Pakistan; and nations the U.S. needs to help manage inward migration, such us Haiti and Guatemala."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem of absent or inexperienced ambassadors goes both ways. It means Washington may not have a capable diplomatic figurehead in these countries to contact in times of need. There are also fewer avenues for host nations to successfully convey messages back to the U.S. administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["When faced with absent ambassadors, amateurish political appointees and deputy mission chiefs who are very junior or career appointees with short resumes, host countries may conclude that they aren’t seen as important to the U.S. and start looking elsewhere for friends."]},{"k":"p","s":["And the U.S. has hollowed out its ambassadorial corps at a time when it is facing growing international influence by the ",["likes of Russia","https://www.rand.org/nsrd/projects/russian-arms-sales-and-sanctions-compliance.html"],", ",["China","https://www.usglc.org/chinas-growing-influence-is-america-getting-left-behind/"]," and Iran – rival nations hoping to capitalize on a perceived diplomatic void left by Washington."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, as the U.S. tries to ",["contain Beijing’s influence","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/a-framework-for-u-s-policy-toward-china-2/"]," in the Asia-Pacific region, Fiji, Indonesia and Laos remain without U.S. ambassadors. Similarly, China’s diplomatic relations with Pakistan – a former key security partner for Washington – have grown while the ambassadorial seat in Islamabad remains empty."]},{"k":"p","s":["And former Soviet states including Georgia and Kazakhstan don’t have U.S. ambassadors even as Russia President Vladimir Putin attempts to consolidate Moscow’s regional influence."]},{"k":"p","s":["In large areas of the world, such as Africa and the Pacific region, and in important areas of policy, the lights may be on in U.S. embassies, but nobody’s home. And that is a distinct problem for national security and strategic interests."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is an updated version of an ",["article originally published","https://theconversation.com/missing-ambassadors-inexperienced-appointees-is-washington-dropping-the-diplomatic-ball-293487?notice=Article+has+been+updated."]," on Oct. 7, 2026."]}],"chars":7639}};
